Aerie-Purpose: Register the sidebar prefs (layout, width, shown) and let the settings page read and write them.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/prefs (browser_prefs.cc, BUILD.gn), chrome/browser/extensions/api/settings_private/prefs_util.cc
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #177. The prefs are aerie.sidebar.layout (a string: sidebar, the default, or horizontal, which
issue #186 will build), aerie.sidebar.width (a number, default 260) and aerie.sidebar.visible (a
boolean, default true). Their names and defaults are in components/aerie_sidebar
(aerie_sidebar_prefs.*). The names are string literals in the settings_private allowlist, as for the
other Aerie prefs, and a test compares them with the constants.

--- a/chrome/browser/prefs/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/prefs/BUILD.gn
@@ -134,6 +134,7 @@
     "//chrome/browser/webauthn",
     "//components/aerie_adblock/browser:guard_prefs",
     "//components/aerie_design_tokens:prefs",
+    "//components/aerie_sidebar:prefs",
     "//components/aerie_tab_model:prefs",
     "//components/aerie_widevine",
     "//components/blocked_content",
